{"name":"Backwater","hex":"#687078","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Backwater","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in the Armidale council area, north-eastern New South Wales, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Backwater"}],"entries":[{"title":"Backwaters (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Backwaters is an album by American guitarist Tony Rice, released in 1982. It is credited to The Tony Rice Unit."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1a/Backwaters_Tony_Rice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backwaters_(album)","wikidata":"Q4839837"},{"title":"Backwater (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Backwater was an American jazz fusion band formed in Mobile, Alabama, active in the 1970s. The band was formed by vocalist and bassist Robby Catlin. After relocating to Birmingham in 1975, the group became known for blending jazz, blues, rock, and Southern musical influences. Its best-known lineup included Catlin, saxophonist Larry Hardin, drummer Scott Pettersen, keyboardist Trippe Thomason, and guitarist Gerry Groom. The band released two independently produced albums: Backwater (1976) and North of the Mason-Dixon and the Heart of Dixie (1978)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Backwater_1976_Birmingham.jpeg/330px-Backwater_1976_Birmingham.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backwater_(band)","wikidata":"Q12053085"},{"title":"Backwater (river)","blocks":[{"text":"A backwater is a relatively stagnant part of a river in which there is little or no current. It can refer to a small anabranch of a main river, which diverges from and meanders alongside the main stem before rejoining it downstreams, and thus carrying a significantly weaker flow; or an ectopic stream pool extend from the side of a watercourse backed up by reverse flow from tides or due to increased flow resistance caused by obstacles such as a weir, dam or levee. Temporary natural obstructions such as ice jams, vegetation blockages, rockslides, debris flow, beaver damming or \"backlogging\" due to downstream flooding can also create backwaters."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backwater_(river)","wikidata":"Q899514"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Saenger_Theatre_Mobile.jpg/500px-Saenger_Theatre_Mobile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Saenger_Theatre_Mobile.jpg/500px-Saenger_Theatre_Mobile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mobile's Saenger Theatre, where Backwater recorded and later reunited in 1997.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaenger_Theatre_Mobile.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Alappuzha_Boat_Beauty_W.jpg/500px-Alappuzha_Boat_Beauty_W.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Alappuzha_Boat_Beauty_W.jpg/1280px-Alappuzha_Boat_Beauty_W.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Alappuzha_Boat_Beauty_W.jpg/500px-Alappuzha_Boat_Beauty_W.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Kerala houseboat in Kumarakom, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlappuzha_Boat_Beauty_W.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/KumarakomHouseBoat.jpg/500px-KumarakomHouseBoat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/KumarakomHouseBoat.jpg/1280px-KumarakomHouseBoat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o